From 35cbc53e739ab3a657b3f4f4761cce855ce213b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 15:10:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 873/913] drivers: stm32_lptimer: fix NULL deref and
 use-after-free in probe
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

counter_dev_alloc() return value was dereferenced without a NULL
check in probe_lpt_device(), causing a NULL pointer dereference on
allocation failure.

In stm32_lptimer_probe(), lpt_dev was read via lpt_dev->pdata.clock
right after stm32_lptimer_free(lpt_dev) freed it on the probe_lpt_device()
error path, causing a use-after-free. Return right after the free
instead of falling through.

Coverity issue: CID 1200193: Read from pointer after free
Coverity issue: CID 1200319: CERT-C Memory Management
Coverity issue: CID 1200555: CERT-C Expression

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 3ab1e4d474df235e18d8fa83e5fd28c865b4cbe1 drivers: stm32_lptimer: fix NULL deref and use-after-free in probe]
Assisted-by: GitHub-Copilot:Claude-Sonnet-5
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I74b3acda15ee0e97dc91576231b671d26b92b487
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/592849
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Fabrice GASNIER <fabrice.gasnier@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
---
 core/drivers/counter/stm32_lptimer.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/drivers/counter/stm32_lptimer.c b/core/drivers/counter/stm32_lptimer.c
index 23ddd3fe4..fc2564c59 100644
--- a/core/drivers/counter/stm32_lptimer.c
+++ b/core/drivers/counter/stm32_lptimer.c
@@ -674,6 +674,9 @@ static TEE_Result probe_lpt_device(struct lptimer_device *lpt_dev)
 
 	if (lpt_dev->pdata.mode & LPTIMER_MODE_COUNTER) {
 		lpt_dev->counter_dev = counter_dev_alloc();
+		if (!lpt_dev->counter_dev)
+			return TEE_ERROR_OUT_OF_MEMORY;
+
 		lpt_dev->counter_dev->ops = &stm32_lpt_counter_ops;
 		lpt_dev->counter_dev->max_ticks = _LPTIM_CNT_MASK;
 		/*
@@ -708,8 +711,10 @@ static TEE_Result stm32_lptimer_probe(const void *fdt, int node,
 	lpt_dev->cdata = compat_data;
 	res = probe_lpt_device(lpt_dev);
 
-	if (res)
+	if (res) {
 		stm32_lptimer_free(lpt_dev);
+		return res;
+	}
 
 	if (clk_enable(lpt_dev->pdata.clock))
 		panic();
-- 
